---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { getBusiness } from '../../lib/content';

const business = await getBusiness();
const locale = 'en';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service — EazyFix"
  description="EazyFix terms of service: quotes, payments, intellectual property, maintenance, liability and withdrawal rights."
  locale={locale}
  business={business}
>
  <h2>1. Provider</h2>
  <p>
    Services are provided by <strong>Georgios Tsouchnikas</strong>, a sole proprietor trading as
    <strong>EazyFix</strong>, Salamina, Greece, VAT number <strong>160020860</strong>.
    Contact: <a href="mailto:info@eazyfix.gr">info@eazyfix.gr</a>, <a href="tel:6971234567">6971234567</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Scope</h2>
  <p>These terms govern computer repair services, website development, app and game development, and maintenance/technical support services.</p>

  <h2>3. Quotes and prices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Quotes are valid for <strong>30 days</strong> from issue unless stated otherwise.</li>
    <li>Prices are in euros. For <strong>business customers</strong> they are shown excluding VAT; for <strong>consumers</strong> they are shown including VAT where required.</li>
    <li>Any domain, hosting and third-party charges are clarified in the quote.</li>
    <li>Additional features or custom requirements are priced separately.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Payment and invoicing</h2>
  <p>Payment terms (deposit, installments, final payment) are agreed in the quote or contract. Invoices are issued in accordance with Greek tax law. Late payments may suspend the service.</p>

  <h2>5. Customer obligations</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Provide timely and accurate information, content and access required for the project.</li>
    <li>Provide timely feedback and approvals.</li>
    <li>Keep backups of their own data unless otherwise agreed.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    Upon full payment, the customer acquires the rights to use the custom deliverables of the project.
    The provider retains the right to showcase the work in their portfolio, as well as rights to
    pre-existing tools, libraries and third-party software (such as open-source packages), which are
    governed by their respective licences.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Third-party services</h2>
  <p>Hosting, domain names, payments and other third-party services are provided under the terms of the respective providers. The provider is not responsible for outages or policy changes of third parties.</p>

  <h2>8. Maintenance and support</h2>
  <p>
    Where monthly maintenance is included, it covers at least backups, uptime monitoring, technical support
    and one (1) change request per month, unless otherwise stated in the quote. Hosting is provided
    according to the project’s needs; any upgrade is charged separately. The monthly fee does not imply a
    minimum commitment unless agreed in writing.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Liability</h2>
  <p>
    The provider makes reasonable efforts regarding quality and availability but does not guarantee
    uninterrupted operation. The provider is not liable for indirect or consequential damages. Total
    liability for contractual claims is limited to the fees paid for the specific service, to the extent
    permitted by law.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Withdrawal (consumers)</h2>
  <p>
    If you are a consumer and the contract is concluded at a distance, you have the right to withdraw within
    <strong>14 days</strong> without justification. This right does not apply, among other cases, to services
    fully performed with your prior express consent, to personalised/custom services, and to digital content
    delivered immediately with consent. To exercise the right: <a href="mailto:info@eazyfix.gr">info@eazyfix.gr</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Online shop</h2>
  <p>
    The website’s online shop is currently not active. When activated, specific terms for sales, VAT-inclusive
    prices, delivery, returns and withdrawal will be added.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These relationships are governed by Greek law. The competent Greek courts have jurisdiction. For consumer
    disputes you may contact the <strong>Hellenic Consumer Ombudsman</strong>
    (<a href="https://www.synigoroskatanaloti.gr" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.synigoroskatanaloti.gr</a>).
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
